.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt NMOUNT 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm nmount
.Nd mount a file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/uio.h
.In sys/mount.h
.Ft int
.Fn nmount "struct iovec *iov" "unsigned int niov" "int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nmount
mounts a file system.
.Fa iov
holds
.Fa niov
/ 2 name and value pairs, each a
.Vt struct iovec ;
a name is a string (its length may include the terminating NUL), a value
may be empty.
The names are:
.Bl -tag -width "from, target"
.It Dv fstype
the file system type:
.Dq tmpfs
or
.Dq nullfs .
Required.
.It Dv fspath
the directory to mount on.
Required.
.It Dv from , target
for
.Dq nullfs ,
the directory to show at
.Dv fspath .
.It Dv nosuid
with an empty value: ignore the set-user-ID and set-group-ID bits of
programs on the file system.
For
.Dq nullfs
this also covers the directory mounted, however it is reached.
.It Dv errmsg
a buffer, of the length its
.Vt iovec
gives, which the kernel fills with a sentence saying why the call failed.
.El
.Pp
.Fa flags
may hold
.Dv MNT_NOSUID ,
the same as the
.Dv nosuid
option, and nothing else: no file system can be mounted read-only yet.
Only the superuser may mount.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std nmount
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EPERM
The caller isn't the superuser.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa niov
is odd, or
.Dv fstype ,
.Dv fspath
or a nullfs
.Dv target
is missing.
.It Bq Er ENODEV
The file system type is unknown.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
An option other than those above, or a flag other than
.Dv MNT_NOSUID ,
was given.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
A directory named doesn't exist.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
One of them isn't a directory.
.It Bq Er ENOSPC
No more file systems can be mounted.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Fn nmount
system call appeared in
.Fx 5.0 .
OxideBSD's takes the same form, with its own system call number and
options.
